# No rules — on purpose. Read before adding one.
#
# The standalone backup viewer is `backup-viewer.html` at the top of `dist`,
# and its canonical URL is the EXTENSIONLESS `/backup-viewer`. Cloudflare Pages
# serves that natively: an HTML asset answers at its extensionless path, and a
# request for `/backup-viewer.html` is redirected (308) to `/backup-viewer`.
# The single-page fallback is native too — with no top-level `404.html` in
# `dist`, every unknown path gets `index.html` — so the app needs no
# `/* /index.html 200` rule either.
#
# The rules that used to live here broke the route on the first real Pages
# release (client-b1, 2026-09-16, Pages run 35160292662): a 200 rewrite
# `/backup-viewer → /backup-viewer.html` handed Pages an `.html` path, which
# Pages answered with its own 308 back to `/backup-viewer` — a redirect loop,
# caught by `scripts/smoke-headers.mjs` after publication. A rewrite whose
# target is an `.html` asset can never work here, and `_redirects` rules are
# only ever proven on a real Pages deployment, never by a unit test — see
# `scripts/backup-viewer-route.test.mjs` for what IS checked in the tree, and
# the smoke for what is checked live.
